{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1097780-spirit-question","id":1097780,"title":"Spirit Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T08:10:24-07:00","id":1097780,"title":"Spirit Question","content":"When attempting to get information from a spirit does it matter if it was slumbering or not?<br /> <br /> IE: Shifter awakens a table spirit and questions the spirit about a conversation that happens at the table before it was awakened. Results: ???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T14:52:31-07:00","id":1097876,"title":"","content":"I would say no. Slumbering means the spirit is sleeping - not active. It should not have any recollection.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, even if there was an active spirit - why would it know anything that happened in the Realm if the spirit was in the umbra? Unless they have a proper charm to know what is happening in the Realm, or unless they were materialized, possessing someone, or otherwise present - the Gauntlet should prevent them from knowing any details of what happened on the other side. Even Peeking only gives you broad overview, not details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T18:58:00-07:00","id":1097932,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is a tricky question. I would say that a Slumbering spirit remembers anything done to its 'home' but not want happened in the vicinity of its 'home'. For example, the spirit of a dining room table could recall every meal served on it or every sexual act performed on it, but it would not remember the conversations during each meal or the foreplay before the sexual acts because its 'home' was not affected by either. The spirit of a bullet might remember the person who chambered the round and the person struck by the bullet, but it would not remember the argument that caused the shooting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T21:03:12-07:00","id":1097968,"title":"","content":"Experiences of the object itself is something I would accept provided such experiences were limited to the interactions the object could conceivably &quot;sense.&quot; <br /> <br /> In most cases, this is going to be tactile - objects know when some person, animal, or another object touches/handles/encounters it. Thus a table might &quot;know&quot; that several objects were placed on it (and eventually provide enough clues to identify that there were two dinner plates, four glasses, and various bowls - but not what was in those dishes, glasses, and bowls like chicken, salad, wine) and that there were people who occasionally touched the table as well. But since a table doesn't have sight, hearing, or smell, wouldn't be able to know anything like that. On the other hand, a smart phone which once recorded picture and sound might very well be to describe all it recorded/sense in complete detail even if the actual video file had been deleted, or even if was never recorded as long as it was &quot;on&quot; at the time.<br /> <br /> In that sense, it is not the &quot;spirit&quot; of the object knowing anything at all. It is what the &quot;object&quot; itself knows, and the newly awakened spirit can communicate it. But much care needs to be taken as to what the object would &quot;know&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T08:49:16-07:00","id":1098110,"title":"","content":"Well, I would add smell and taste to that list as well, as the chemicals from food aromas and food spills will permeate the materials of most tables. Of course, the spirit will not have a reference point, so it may be difficult for the players to understand the difference between the smell of tomato soup and the taste of a drop of fat from a hamburger that was spilled on the table (try explaining the smell of tomato soup or the taste of hamburger without referring to other flavors or smells and you will see what I mean).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:26:46-07:00","id":1098140,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow any smell unless the objects were known as something that strongly retains smells, and only in cases where the smell retention was prolonged (say a box of chocolate kept inside a box, perfume kept in a drawer, or objects inside a particularly moldy house/room or which suffered smoke damage from fire). Typically it would be softer goods like sofas, clothing, and other upholstery and textiles and such which retain smells, not so much hard goods. Taste would be even more restrictive, requiring the object to essentially have &quot;consumed&quot; the item. Unless it was something like clothing and stains, I'd be leery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}